lines=['# ATAX: complete CH/DH P0, F128, F256 matched evidence','', '**Conclusion:** F256 improves DH itself by1.7823% in reciprocal-cycle speed and1.7511% in cycle reduction. The relative improvement I=1.112797 does not mean DH has passed CH: CH/DH=0.992325, so DH still takes0.7735% more cycles. A large contribution to I is CH deterioration: CH cycles increase9.3310% from P0 while DH cycles decrease1.7511%. F128 remains a negative DH self-response and is retained.','', 'This is six closed sources for one frozen input, not a suite GM or per-program best-parameter selection. All six retain their original accepted scientific roles; two new CH points passed an independent frozen read-only strict/true164/native-restore audit. No remaining live job was read for this analysis, and no simulation, registration, controller/owner/budget/source change or manuscript edit was made.','', '## Identity, authority and actual capture contract','', 'Frozen input digest: `eededb785179fc0488c5a01d95154f6748ea45a2ea7bb18ecdbc316cf5166950`; ROI `5ba85e56ae33e604c38407d5d8641078cb0a1b06aaaa9928cc0de4c61d94f442`. This is the full two-kernel declared eededb capture, not the separate ATAX1of10/trim identity. Actual body qualification, strict proof and bounded headers agree: K1 `_Z12atax_kernel1PfS_S_`,71,380,992active-thread instructions; K2 `_Z12atax_kernel2PfS_S_`,74,285,056. Each has grid(16,1,1),block(256,1,1),16CTAs, stream0; total145,666,048instructions/32CTAs. These values are read from this input\'s own contract, not inferred from workload names.','', 'Fixed Core `9eedb3131937748f0492fa83aad37d3691118d70`, Framework `02775fd795cde5aae1480d81cee6eb481d0a08f4`, simulator binary SHA `02a289360b42a573832698c978f21ad2125182a453067a35be60410f1eb8888d`. PhaseI authority remains `361fa6fa0700825bb9cda43e25b9fd1f60e0b262`; StageII authorized contract `5001c3f35052f7f91f1ad41eeff83f2947a0878d`. Original CH-P0/DH-P0/DH-F128/DH-F256 are selected by full digest/cell/profile from ORIGINAL_REFERENCE_INDEX.json, not substituted by name from R2/IR/EP/PQPS. Existing reference aliases are disclosed rather than promoted.','', 'The frozen prior F128 four-source packet manifest is `af69366bb4fe44dd919518150f763a248451a4cdd67a4764c25b2494bec47158`; all its member SHA remain unchanged. Its four RESULT identities exactly match the new six-source packet. The new CH-F256 has UUID `3b949083-a0f8-4778-92f1-d940c66acfe6`.','', '## Whole-replay performance and relative-improvement decomposition','',tab(['Design','P0 cycles','F128 cycles','F256 cycles'],[[c,*[by[c,p]['cycles']for p in['P0','F128','F256']]]for c in['CH','DH']]),'',tab(['Profile','S_CH=CH0/CH_F','S_DH=DH0/DH_F','CH_F/DH_F','I=S_DH/S_CH','DH extra cycles vs CH_F %'],[[p['profile'],p['S_CH'],p['S_DH'],p['R_variant'],p['I'],100*(p['DH_cycles_over_CH_variant']-1)]for p in performance]),'', 'F256 I factorization: `1.112797 = 1.093310 (CH cycle-regression factor) * 1.017823 (DH self-speedup)`. This prevents relative-benefit improvement from being presented as an11.28% DH self-speedup. In log-ratio bookkeeping,83.47% of the increase in log(I) comes from the CH regression factor; that is an arithmetic decomposition, not a fraction of runtime or causal attribution. For F128, CH worsens5.1119% and DH worsens0.0452%; its positive I therefore comes from CH worsening more.','', '## Kernel location','',tab(['Design/profile','K1 cycles','K2 cycles','Total','K1 delta vs same-design P0','K2 delta vs P0'],[[c+'-'+p,by[c,p]['kernels'][0]['cycles'],by[c,p]['kernels'][1]['cycles'],by[c,p]['cycles'],by[c,p]['kernels'][0]['cycles']-by[c,'P0']['kernels'][0]['cycles'],by[c,p]['kernels'][1]['cycles']-by[c,'P0']['kernels'][1]['cycles']]for c,p in pairs]),'', 'CH-F256 regression2,652,708cycles splits K1+2,652,012 and K2+696. DH-F256 improvement558,265cycles splits K1-558,503 and K2+238. Thus almost all net change is localized to K1, while K2 changes are small and adverse. It would be inaccurate to say K2 is exactly unchanged. F128 follows the same localization pattern but has opposite DH sign.','', '## Read/write traffic and visible admission events','', 'Units: L2 GLOBAL accepted reads and misses are32-byte sectors; accepted excludes reservation retries and equals HIT+HIT_RESERVED+MISS+SECTOR_MISS. GLOBAL misses=MISS+SECTOR_MISS. DRAM read/write values are issued32-byte data atoms across20controllers, not necessarily the same access population as GLOBAL reads. All-L2 misses include write-related access types; their count must not be relabeled GLOBAL read misses.','']
